<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Identity invariants, 2026 ~ sync carries, verification decides

The operator un-asked a founding choice on 2026-10-20: //"When we started, all we had was direct API calls and CRDT docs, so that's where I put everything that should auto-sync based on the capabilities of the currently-in-context keys. But does setting these identity invariants on a mutable CRDT read pono?"// A Codex seat read the code and a Copilot seat read the field, each in two traded waves. Claims read MEASURED (read in code, with file and line) or LEAD (inference, or a recalled source). The ruling stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`>> #/rulings, //sync carries; verification decides//.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! Findings

# ''The gate verifies continuity, never selection'' (both seats, MEASURED). The Binding Gate walks the persona KEL to its head, verifies the countersigned edge, requires an epoch and reads the shadow (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:123-177`), for the KEL prefix the caller hands it. Boot takes the PersonaGroup, signer, edge and prefix from the worn mount, else from plain daemon-doc tiddlers (`open-node-vessel.ts:1812-1882`; `open-browser-vessel.ts:1185,1241`); the gate leaves the PersonaGroup and the cabal doc outside its proof (`:43`, `:180`). A coherent foreign bundle passes the chain's own checks unless a local commitment names the face a vessel wears.
# ''The lease frontier carries no authority of its own'' (Codex, MEASURED). The fold accepts any integer under the prefix, with no signature or writer check (`epoch-lease.ts:31`; `lease-rekey.ts:47`): a forged high slot denies; a deletion or a stale replica lowers the observed maximum, and an old edge reads current against it.
# ''Plane URLs carry structure, not a binding'' (both, MEASURED). Membership and URLs come from the local bootstrap by a group-derived name (`persona-planes.ts:154`), with no signed founding or admission act behind each.
# ''The house already holds the right pattern'' (both, MEASURED). The KEL board carries signed events in mutable carriage, and its reader folds them and exposes forks rather than taking a winner (`persona-kel-board.ts:50,173`); dyads verify on read; the cabal doc left identity for affiliation.
# ''The field agrees'' (Copilot, LEAD from recalled sources). KERI, Keybase, Certificate Transparency and signed Git keep authority in signed append-only history; Matrix keeps device lists and indexes in mutable sync, signed on read; Signal keeps a sealed local trust root per device.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-sort`>>

!! The sort ~ where each pin rests

|! Pin |! Its home |
| PersonaGroup, persona-KEL prefix (the selectors) | the sealed identity anchor, written only by founding, admission and recovery |
| device edge, signer, hearth true name | signed records, verified on read; the edge already carries the true name |
| lease epochs | signed advances in the per-writer shape, beside a sealed local frontier that never falls |
| dyads | a CRDT of signed entries, verified on read |
| plane URLs and membership | signed founding and admission acts, projected into the planes |
| the group secret's seal | a sealed custody row |
| the cabal doc, the catalog, working content | shared mutable CRDT, with access checks at use |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/recommendation`>>

!! The recommendation ~ both seats converged

A sealed anchor per face per device; signed records carried by sync under immutable ids and verified against the anchor and the KEL; the face planes as verified projections; per-vessel records off the mirrored daemon doc; summonses on `@intents`. In-context keys and held grants decide what a vessel may //receive//; the anchor decides which face it //wears//; verification decides what //counts//.

''Reds'': a forged selector row, and a coherent valid foreign bundle, switch no pinned face, and a missing anchor refuses boot; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork; a deleted, replayed or forged epoch never lowers the local frontier; reordering face rows moves no pin from its owner on either host; a join bootstraps offline from its admission bundle and the anchor; the floor gains no face authority from an unverified pin; capability-driven sync still converges every plane that carries no authority.

<<~/ahu>>

